{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"CodeInspectus Setup"},"description":"Inspect external-engine health and exact platform download sizes, save declined choices, or install selected Opengrep/Gitleaks/Trivy/OSV-Scanner components after explicit confirmation. Pass path (the repository to scan) to plan or install only the OSV vulnerability databases for the ecosystems its lockfiles use (and GitHub Actions advisories when it has workflows); each is listed with an estimated size (integrity: TLS + recorded SHA-256, OSV publishes no signature), and osv_ecosystems pins the exact list the user approved. Plan is offline. Install writes only to ~/.codeinspectus, verifies immutable pins/publisher provenance for engines, and never modifies the target repository.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"default":"plan","description":"Plan is offline/read-only. Install downloads only after confirm_downloads=true. Decline saves the choice. Update answers a database_update yes: without confirm_downloads it returns the offline update plan; with it, it downloads the installed databases' updates. Snooze answers not now or not for a week (pass snooze).","enum":["plan","install","decline","update","snooze"],"type":"string"},"components":{"description":"Components to install or decline. Default: all four external engines.","items":{"enum":["opengrep","gitleaks","trivy","osv-scanner"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"confirm_downloads":{"description":"Must be true for an install that needs network downloads.","type":"boolean"},"confirm_large_downloads":{"description":"With action=update: must also be true when the update plan lists a database over 100 MB (large_downloads). Pass it only after the user gave a separate yes for those downloads.","type":"boolean"},"osv_ecosystems":{"description":"Exact OSV ecosystem databases the user approved, e.g. [\"npm\", \"PyPI\"]. Overrides the detection from path. Omitted or empty (an empty list is no list): the databases path needs (none without path), plus a refresh of any installed database that went stale. To download no OSV database, leave osv-scanner out of components.","items":{"enum":["npm","PyPI","Packagist","Go","crates.io","RubyGems","Maven","NuGet","Pub","GitHub Actions"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Absolute path to the repository the user wants to scan. Only the OSV vulnerability databases for ecosystems whose lockfiles are found there (read-only, by file name) are offered.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"skip_large_downloads":{"description":"With action=update and confirm_downloads=true: refresh only the databases under 100 MB and leave out those the update plan lists in large_downloads (when the user declined them). The prompt then comes back as after a partial update.","type":"boolean"},"snooze":{"description":"With action=snooze: not_now asks again in 24 hours, not_for_a_week in 7 days.","enum":["not_now","not_for_a_week"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"codeinspectus_setup","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"message":{"type":"string"},"next_step":{"type":"string"},"outcome":{"enum":["planned","installed","declined","updated","update_partial","update_failed","snoozed"],"type":"string"},"plan":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"components":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["none","download","redownload","refresh_database","blocked"],"type":"string"},"coverage":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"download_size_bytes":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"estimated_database_disk_bytes":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"id":{"enum":["opengrep","gitleaks","trivy","osv-scanner"],"type":"string"}